          "kicker": "Discipline problem",
          "heading": "Bill Sweeney says England must cut yellow cards after Six Nations sin-binnings",
          "body": "Discipline is on the agenda before Sunday's meeting with Australia, the opener of England's November campaign. England picked up eight yellow cards and one red across their five Six Nations matches, playing 118 minutes at less than a full complement. Sweeney says analysis suggests England drop to eighth or ninth best in the world when down to 14 players, and that Steve Borthwick is working with the squad on it. \"It has been a big internal discussion,\" Sweeney said."
