    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-05",
      "edition": "Thursday 5 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Autumn outlook",
          "heading": "Tom English expects competitive All Blacks defeat, then wins over Australia and Japan",
          "body": "BBC Sport's Tom English expects Scotland to lose a competitive contest with New Zealand on Saturday, then beat Australia and Japan, though he would not rule out three wins from three. He points to the recent record: Scotland trailed 17-0 the last time they met the All Blacks and were 14-0 down the time before. His warning is that Dave Rennie's side are at their wiliest when the heat comes on, and Scotland start to make mistakes at the breakdown and lineout."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "All Blacks drop tighthead Tyrel Lomax from tour squad",
          "body": "Costelow set to start at fly-half for Wales against Japan."
        }
