    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-05",
      "edition": "Thursday 5 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coach's priorities",
          "heading": "Contepomi says a Dublin win would be a bonus, with performance first",
          "body": "Felipe Contepomi puts performance ahead of the result for Friday's test, saying Argentina's first task is to be competitive. Argentina have never beaten Ireland away from home in 11 meetings, and the coach said ending that run is not the chief motivator. \"It would mean a lot, but I think more so it is for us to try to get better,\" he said. Contepomi said the 28-24 win over the Lions at the Aviva in June 2025 offers little, since every game starts from zero."
        },
        {
