    "461": {
      "date": "2026-11-05",
      "edition": "Thursday 5 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Bledisloe fallout",
          "heading": "Angus Bell says Wallabies have fixed Bledisloe problems ahead of England Test",
          "body": "Prop Angus Bell says the Wallabies have fixed what went wrong against the All Blacks, whose quick ball and fast breakdown exposed their movement speed in two heavy defeats that ended a six-game unbeaten run. Bell says the changes have been implemented at training. Australia sit third in the South on nine points, behind New Zealand and South Africa, the only undefeated sides on 15. Asked what success looks like, Bell answered \"Three from three,\" with Scotland and Wales still to come after England."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "All Blacks drop tighthead Tyrel Lomax from tour squad",
          "body": "Costelow set to start at fly-half for Wales against Japan."
        }
